AB  - Evaluated the effect on well-being and sickness certification of interviews and 3 dialogue sessions concerning ideas about pain in young immigrants suffering from long standing, benign pain. A randomized clinical 4-wk trial was conducted between 2 treatment groups at a primary health care center in Stockholm, Sweden. Ss were 92 persons (aged 25–45 yrs) on sick leave of more than 6 wks. 45 immigrants, mean age 38 years, mean sick leave 13 months, completed the program. There were no significant differences in general or diagnostic data between the treatment groups. All had pain. Three-quarters reported pain anxiety. Nearly half had depressive disorders. Only 10 persons had self-rated ability for part-time work. After the program, there were significant differences in favour of the experimental group in number of participants with pain anxiety, with diagnosed depression, with self-rated work ability, and in the number of participants who had returned to work at the 8-mo follow-up. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
